  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "The lengths of two line segments are \\(a\\) units and \\(b\\) units respectively. Then the correct relation between them is:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{a+b}{2}\\gt\\sqrt{ab}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{a+b}{2}\\lt\\sqrt{ab}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{a+b}{2}=\\sqrt{ab}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{a+b}{2}\\le\\sqrt{ab}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{a+b}{2}\\ge\\sqrt{ab}\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "e",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1953-p45.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Since \\[ (a-b)^2\\ge0, \\] we have \\((a+b)^2\\ge4ab.\\) Both sides are nonnegative, so \\[ \\frac{a+b}{2}\\ge\\sqrt{ab}. \\] Equality occurs when \\(a=b.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is E.",
      "hints": [
        "Start with the nonnegative square \\((a-b)^2\\)",
        "Equality must remain possible when the two segment lengths are equal"
      ],
